1
00:03:07,826 --> 00:03:13,826
Grief. Anger. Vengeance.

2
00:06:15,652 --> 00:06:21,652
The Head Hunter is a horror, fantasy film directed by Jordan Downey.

3
00:09:23,478 --> 00:09:29,478
On the outskirts of a kingdom, a quiet but fierce medieval warrior
protects the realm from monsters and the occult.

4
00:12:31,304 --> 00:12:37,304
His gruesome collection of heads is missing only one - the
monster that killed his daughter years ago.

5
00:15:39,130 --> 00:15:45,130
Driven by a thirst for revenge, he travels wild expanses on horseback.

6
00:18:46,956 --> 00:18:52,956
When his second chance arrives, it’s in a way far
more horrifying than he ever imagined.

7
00:21:54,782 --> 00:22:00,782
Father, played by Christopher Rygh.

8
00:25:02,608 --> 00:25:08,608
Daughter, played by Cora Kaufman.

9
00:28:10,434 --> 00:28:16,434
The Head (Voice), played by Aisha Ricketts.

10
00:31:18,260 --> 00:31:24,260
The Head Hunter, originally titled The Head, is a 2018 American independent fantasy
horror film directed, written, produced and edited by Jordan Downey.

11
00:34:26,086 --> 00:34:32,086
It stars Norwegian actor Christopher Rygh, Cora Kaufman, and Aisha Ricketts.

12
00:37:33,913 --> 00:37:39,913
The film centers on the title character, who works as a bounty hunter for a local kingdom, all the
while he awaits the eventual return of the creature that murdered his daughter.

13
00:40:41,739 --> 00:40:47,739
Influenced by Quest for Fire, The Witch, The X-Files, and Tales From the
Crypt, The Head Hunter was developed by Downey and Kevin Stewart.

14
00:43:49,565 --> 00:43:55,565
The filming location was decided long before the story was developed.

15
00:46:57,391 --> 00:47:03,391
The concept was developed at a writer's retreat, in which the filmmakers had assembled and hosted
at Stewart's family home in Soutelo Mourisco, a small village in Northern Portugal.

16
00:50:05,217 --> 00:50:11,217
Rygh, in his feature-film debut, was cast in the leading role after
the filmmakers discovered him on a casting website.

17
00:53:13,043 --> 00:53:19,043
Principal photography began in Bragança, Portugal, while
additional scenes were shot in Norway, and California.

18
00:56:20,869 --> 00:56:26,869
The Head Hunter premiered at the Sitges Film Festival on October 6,
2018, as a part of the "Panorama Fantàstic" section.

19
00:59:28,695 --> 00:59:34,695
While the film was screened under the title The Head at Sitges and Nightmares Film
Festival, but was later changed to The Head Hunter due to lukewarm reactions.

20
01:02:36,521 --> 01:02:42,521
The film received several awards and nominations at various film festivals and received positive reviews from critics upon its release, with
many praising the film's atmosphere, cinematography, and Rygh's performance, although its low budget prompted some criticism.

21
01:05:44,347 --> 01:05:50,347
The film explores themes of monster, grave, castle, woods, revenge.

22
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
The tone is dark.
